From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ship OpenFST's and pybind11's licences in the wheel's
 dist-info

cmake/openfst.cmake FetchContent-downloads csukuangfj/openfst
v1.8.5-2026-04-10 at build time (the repo carries no OpenFST source of
its own) and links its fst and fstscript libraries, built static, into
_kaldifst - the one extension module every wheel ships.
cmake/pybind11.cmake likewise FetchContent-downloads pybind11 v3.0.0,
whose headers are compiled into that same module.

setup.py declares no `license_files`, so setuptools' default
LICEN[CS]E* root glob is what ships kaldifst's own LICENSE; it never
reaches OpenFST's COPYING (Apache-2.0) or pybind11's LICENSE
(BSD-3-Clause), which only exist in the build tree after CMake's
FetchContent runs. Reproduced against the real
kaldifst-1.8.0-cp312-cp312-manylinux_2_26_aarch64.manylinux_2_28_aarch64.whl
from PyPI: dist-info/licenses/ carries only LICENSE.

Restoring both texts unchanged from those tags at the project root as
LICENSE.openfst and LICENSE.pybind11 is picked up by that same default
glob with no packaging change, landing them in dist-info/licenses/
alongside kaldifst's own LICENSE.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; no fork of k2-fsa/kaldifst to push from]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 LICENSE.openfst  | 13 +++++++++++++
 LICENSE.pybind11 | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 42 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.openfst
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.pybind11

diff --git a/LICENSE.openfst b/LICENSE.openfst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d0d7ee0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSE.openfst
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
